(5059947, 735859, 76162, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all of your comments!<br/>True the background was not good, its actually a t-shirt :) obviously not ironed...<br/>I was just in a hurry to shoot it while my smoking friends were around and with them the cigars(I don''t smoke). Something dark and shiny would be my choice if I had any in my kitchen at the time...<br/>Its not possible to make the smoke come out of the mouth, eye sockets are the only holes in the scull.</td>', 'Thanks for all of your comments!True the background was not good, its actually a t-shirt :) obviously not ironed...I was just in a hurry to shoot it while my smoking friends were around and with them the cigars(I don''t smoke). Something dark and shiny would be my choice if I had any in my kitchen at the time...Its not possible to make the smoke come out of the mouth, eye sockets are the only holes in the scull.', '2008-11-12 13:17:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5060133, 735973, 29011, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Davenit:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>I actually went back and reshot the image I''m using in the series after the challenge had started. I just wasn''t thrilled with the outcome. So I suffered through tons of incense lung and got the image I wanted. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''m totally thrilled you got the willpower to go back and reshoot to get the shot you wanted. That''s a great feeling. Though I''ve done 4 smoke shots myself, I''m not a big fan of incense. With match pics, friends and family who come in later think I burnt my food again LOL. So I can imagine what you where going through. The smell does tend to stick around.</td>', 'Originally posted by Davenit: I actually went back and reshot the image I''m using in the series after the challenge had started. I just wasn''t thrilled with the outcome. So I suffered through tons of incense lung and got the image I wanted.   I''m totally thrilled you got the willpower to go back and reshoot to get the shot you wanted. That''s a great feeling. Though I''ve done 4 smoke shots myself, I''m not a big fan of incense. With match pics, friends and family who come in later think I burnt my food again LOL. So I can imagine what you where going through. The smell does tend to stick around.', '2008-11-12 14:20:53.000000', NULL, 0),
